This project is a fork of PlanSys2 (ROS2 Planning System),
originally developed by Francisco Martín Rico, Jonatan Ginés Clavero,
Francisco J. Rodríguez Lera, and Vicente Matellán Olivera.

  Original repository: https://github.com/PlanSys2/ros2_planning_system
  Original license:    Apache License, Version 2.0
  Original reference:  F. Martín et al., "PlanSys2: A Planning System
                       Framework for ROS2", IROS 2021.

Most of the plansys2_* packages included in this repository come from the
original PlanSys2 project and remain subject to its copyright notices and
the Apache License, Version 2.0. They are carried with their upstream
history rather than copied, so `git log` on any file shows what came from
PlanSys2 and what did not. Which packages those are, and which are
original to this repository, is set out below.

The ones that come from PlanSys2 are not reproduced unmodified. Every one
of them has been changed here, and the changes fall into four kinds:

  Extension points. plansys2_msgs carries the epistemic fields of
  PlanItem, which are what lets a policy travel in a Plan, and the
  outcome field of ActionExecution, which is what lets a performer
  report what it observed. plansys2_executor loads behavior tree nodes
  named by parameter and publishes an observed outcome on a port. These
  are additions: a classical planner sets none of the fields and a
  classical performer fills none of them in.

  Bring-up. plansys2_bringup starts the epistemic state and perception
  nodes on opt-in launch arguments, and plansys2_lifecycle_manager
  manages them alongside the original four.

  Portability. Shims that let one source tree build on both Humble and
  Rolling, chiefly around ament_index_cpp and the ROS executor and QoS
  APIs, gathered in plansys2_core.

  Fixes. Defects found while running the system, repaired in place
  rather than worked around from outside.

plansys2_tui_cli is an upstream package extended further than the rest:
it gains the `ros2 plansys2 epistemic` verb and a Textual dashboard, and
it vendors the Textual library as described below.

plansys2_tests carries two missions of its own, test_5 and test_6, which
exercise the epistemic execution path end to end.

These packages are original to this repository and contain no PlanSys2
code:

  plansys2_epistemic_planner        plansys2_epddl_grounder
  plansys2_epistemic_executor       plansys2_epistemic_bt_builder
  plansys2_epistemic_msgs           plansys2_epistemic_perception
  plansys2_aletheia_plan_solver     eplansys, eplansys_docs

They are named plansys2_* where they plug into a PlanSys2 extension
point, so that the package name says what it attaches to. The name does
not indicate origin; this list does.

Those original packages were developed as part of a terminal work at the
Instituto Politécnico Nacional, Mexico, and are also distributed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The package plansys2_epistemic_planner contains, in its planning core,
code derived from the Aletheia epistemic planner: the Kripke state
representation, DEL product update, bisimulation contraction, formula
representation and model checking, heuristics, search strategies, the
selection policy, the parser and the validator. Aletheia is a work of
the same author and is incorporated here in process rather than invoked
as a binary; plansys2_aletheia_plan_solver runs that binary instead.

  Source:  https://github.com/HanielUlises/Aletheia
  License: Apache License, Version 2.0

The remaining files of that package - the plan solver plugin, the policy
plan serialisation, the action mapping and the formula text front end -
are original to this repository.

The package plansys2_epddl_grounder includes three files copied verbatim
from other projects, both used at run time rather than compiled:

  libraries/intermediate.epddl
    The "intermediate" EPDDL action-type library, from the plank
    toolkit by Alessandro Burigana and Francesco Fabiano.
    Source:  https://github.com/HanielUlises/plank
    License: MIT

  examples/muddy-children-domain.epddl
  examples/muddy-children-problem.epddl
    EPDDL sources from the epddl-workspace of Epistemic-Robotics.
    Source:  https://github.com/HanielUlises/Epistemic-Robotics
    License: Apache License, Version 2.0

The package plansys2_tui_cli vendors the Textual terminal UI library
under plansys2_tui_cli/vendor/textual, so that the command line front
end runs without a pip install into the ROS environment:

  plansys2_tui_cli/vendor/textual/
    The Textual TUI framework by Will McGugan and contributors.
    Source:  https://github.com/Textualize/textual
    License: MIT, reproduced verbatim in that directory's LICENSE file.

It is vendored unmodified and is excluded from this repository's linters
for that reason.

plank itself is not vendored. It is fetched and built from source
through dependency_repos.repos and invoked as a subprocess; its MIT
license applies to that build.

